Title: Difference-in-differences with fractional filtering
Abstract: When programs select units after setbacks that fade gradually, differential untreated recovery can violate ordinary parallel trends. This note replaces first differencing with fractional filtering under a filtered mean balance assumption. Explicit autoregressive models show when this restriction holds while parallel trends fails; assistance after local labor-market downturns illustrates its potential. The filtered group difference identifies the first-period average treatment effect on the treated and a distributed-lag effect subsequently. Untreated pretreatment data can help choose the filter, supporting sensitivity analysis.
